  "term": "trigeminal nucleus",
  "definition": "The trigeminal nucleus is any of four brainstem nerve-cell groups associated with the fifth cranial nerve. These include the principal sensory nucleus, mesencephalic nucleus, spinal trigeminal tract, and motor nucleus.",
